3309:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/ssl_tls12_client.c ****      * Taking shortcut here. We assume that the server always allows the
3310:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/ssl_tls12_client.c ****      * PRF Hash function and has sent it in the allowed signature
3311:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/ssl_tls12_client.c ****      * algorithms list received in the Certificate Request message.
3312:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/ssl_tls12_client.c ****      *
3313:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/ssl_tls12_client.c ****      * Until we encounter a server that does not, we will take this
3314:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/ssl_tls12_client.c ****      * shortcut.
3315:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/ssl_tls12_client.c ****      *
3316:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/ssl_tls12_client.c ****      * Reason: Otherwise we should have running hashes for SHA512 and
3317:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/ssl_tls12_client.c ****      *         SHA224 in order to satisfy 'weird' needs from the server
3318:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/ssl_tls12_client.c ****      *         side.
3319:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/ssl_tls12_client.c ****      */
